Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 4.3  Red knot \[LongDash] monthly population centroid restricted to \
the Americas flyway. Compare this coherent loop with the broken global \
centroid (the ",
 StyleBox["knotGlobal",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " contrast above), which would sit uselessly in the mid-Atlantic, ~4,670 \
km/month from this track. ",
 StyleBox["A caveat in the other direction:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " presence weighting blunts but does not erase effort bias. The Americas \
winter centroid here sits around Panama/northern Colombia rather than at the \
iconic ",
 StyleBox["rufa",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " wintering grounds in Tierra del Fuego (~54\[Degree]S): the densely-birded \
USA and Caribbean still outweigh the sparsely-observed Patagonian coast, and \
the centroid blends several wintering areas. The shape of the journey is \
right; the precise southern extreme is pulled north."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"460d1e0e-a21c-4ed0-856b-43edd280a2ea"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.  Animating the population centroid", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"9ecfdcc5-1136-472e-aaca-a31090e01408"],

Cell["\<\
Stringing the twelve monthly centroids together and interpolating along great \
circles between them turns the static loops of \[Section]4 into the animated \
comet-trail globe shown at the top of this post. Each species' centre of mass \
glides through the year over its faint annual route \[LongDash] the most \
compact possible summary of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]where is this population, \
right now, on average.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"9b9a20c8-4541-4bb7-921d-1e4c0c0e24a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can also quantify each loop. Summing the great-circle distances between \
consecutive monthly centroids (over observed months only) gives the ",
 StyleBox["annual centroid displacement",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] how far the centre of mass travels in a year:"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"f920b72c-076e-483c-9a50-71d42d70338e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Annual centroid displacement per primary flyway track. *)
pl = Import[FileNameJoin[{$BFPDataDir, \"path_lengths.csv\"}], \"CSV\"];
prim = Select[Rest[pl], ! StringContainsQ[#[[3]], \"global\", IgnoreCase -> \
True] &];
BarChart[prim[[All, 4]],
   ChartLabels -> (Style[#[[2]] <> \"\\n(\" <> #[[3]] <> \")\", 10] & /@ prim),
   BarOrigin -> Left,
   PlotLabel -> Style[
     \"Annual centroid displacement (km) -- NOT individual journey \
distance\", 13],
   ImageSize -> 780, AspectRatio -> 0.5]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"e800ad2a-3b7b-4523-b126-e994e571c990"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
