Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 6.2  Day length experienced along each centroid track through the \
year. The Arctic tern, following summer from one hemisphere to the other, \
sits under a ~19 h midsummer day at its breeding latitudes \[LongDash] more \
daylight over the year than any other animal. Whether day length actually ",
 StyleBox["paces",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the speed in Figure 6.1, however, our 12-point series cannot establish \
(see the photoperiod test above)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"12725a7f-f831-4e0a-86ec-223d2364f9b1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7.  The energy of migration", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"49876651-47c8-4ea9-ba94-34a844f0d8ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cheap per kilometre, ruinous per year.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Flapping flight is one of the most energetically expensive activities in \
nature per unit time, yet astonishingly ",
 StyleBox["cheap per kilometre",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] a migrating bird converts fat to distance with an efficiency \
no land animal approaches. The catch is the sheer length of the journey: a \
cost-per-kilometre that looks trivial becomes an enormous annual fuel bill \
when multiplied by tens of thousands of kilometres."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"7609120d-fdb1-4bb5-9704-5ca2b86c5a59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The model.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " We estimate flight power with the standard ",
 StyleBox["Pennycuick flapping-flight model",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Pennycuick 2008), which sums three terms: ",
 StyleBox["induced power",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (the cost of generating lift, dominant at low speed), ",
 StyleBox["parasite power",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (drag on the body, dominant at high speed), and ",
 StyleBox["profile power",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (drag on the flapping wings). Their sum is the classic U-shaped power \
curve, whose two landmark speeds are the ",
 StyleBox["minimum-power speed ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["V",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 StyleBox["mp",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (cheapest per hour, where you would loiter) and the higher ",
 StyleBox["maximum-range speed ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["V",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 StyleBox["mr",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (cheapest per kilometre, where the tangent from the origin touches the \
curve). A bird minimising the fuel needed to cover distance should cruise \
near ",
 StyleBox["V",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 StyleBox["mr",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " \[LongDash] and that is the speed at which we evaluate the fuel cost below."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"a284fb3e-a347-424b-a8d1-096926fc00a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For our three species the model gives a max-range speed ",
 StyleBox["V",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 StyleBox["mr",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " of about ",
 StyleBox["49 km/h",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Arctic tern), ",
 StyleBox["48 km/h",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (common swift), and ",
 StyleBox["59 km/h",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (red knot), with a cost of transport of roughly ",
 StyleBox["0.25, ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["0.12, and ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["0.41 kJ/km",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " respectively. Expressed as fuel, each 1,000 km of flight burns about ",
 StyleBox["5.9%, ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["7.9%, and ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["7.7%",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of body mass respectively \[LongDash] which is why a long-haul migrant can \
nearly double its weight in fat before departure."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"132ea343-d376-43e0-a71b-9383781f9729"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Pennycuick flapping-flight power at speed V (level, still air).
   Abbreviated from wolfram/energetics.wls. *)
rho = 1.225; g = 9.81;            (* air density, gravity *)
Sb[m_] := 0.00813 m^0.666;        (* body frontal area (Pennycuick) *)
Pind[m_, b_, V_] := 2 (m g)^2 / (V rho Pi b^2);          (* induced  *)
Ppar[m_, b_, V_] := 0.5 rho V^3 Sb[m] 0.10;              (* parasite *)
Ppro[m_, V_]     := 1.2 (1.05/8.4) (m g)^1.5 / Sqrt[rho Sb[m]];  (* profile \
*)
Ptot[m_, b_, V_] := Pind[m, b, V] + Ppar[m, b, V] + Ppro[m, V];
Vmr[m_, b_] := V /. Last @ Minimize[{Ptot[m, b, V]/V, V > 5}, V];\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"b8b1ed89-9b29-42ae-aa26-bd0415ab9ea8"],

